/*
Problem: Process String with Special Characters (LC 3612)
Topic: String Simulation

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Traverse the string one character at
a time.

Depending on the character:

• Lowercase letter:
  Append it to the answer.

• '*':
  Remove the last character.

• '#':
  Duplicate the current string.

• Any other character:
  Reverse the current string.

Simulate each operation in order.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Initialize an empty string.

2. Traverse every character.

3. Perform:

   • Letter  -> Append.

   • '*'     -> Remove last character
                (if possible).

   • '#'     -> Duplicate the string.

   • Others  -> Reverse the string.

4. Return the final string.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

s = "ab#"

Process:

"a"

"ab"

"abab"

Answer:

"abab"

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

s = "abc*"

Process:

"a"

"ab"

"abc"

"ab"

Answer:

"ab"

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

s = "abc%"

Process:

"a"

"ab"

"abc"

Reverse

"cba"

Answer:

"cba"

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Each character represents exactly one
operation on the current string.

Processing them sequentially produces
the required final string.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n + k)

n = Length of input string.

k = Cost of duplicate/reverse
operations.

Worst case can reach O(n²).

Space : O(n)

Stores the resulting string.

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

String Simulation
*/

class Solution {
public:
    string processStr(string s) {

        string ans = "";

        for (char ch : s) {

            // Append letter
            if ('a' <= ch && ch <= 'z') {

                ans.push_back(ch);
            }

            // Remove last character
            else if (ch == '*' &&
                     !ans.empty()) {

                ans.pop_back();
            }

            // Duplicate string
            else if (ch == '#') {

                ans += ans;
            }

            // Reverse string
            else {

                reverse(ans.begin(),
                        ans.end());
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
